---
import LegalLayout from '~/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '~/data/site';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`The terms that govern use of the ${site.name} website and the services offered through it.`}
  updated="26 September 2026"
>
  <h2>Agreement</h2>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of this website. Work we perform for you is governed by a separate
    signed contract or proposal, which takes precedence over anything on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Estimates and proposals</h2>
  <p>
    Figures shown on this site, including savings ranges, paybacks and capacity guidance, are
    illustrative. They are not offers and not guarantees. A binding price comes only from a written
    proposal issued after a site assessment, and remains valid for the period stated on it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Savings and production estimates depend on weather, occupancy, utility tariffs, equipment
    condition and regulation, all of which change. Actual results will differ.
  </p>

  <h2>Payments</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Online payments are processed by a third-party provider under their own terms.</li>
    <li>Invoices are due on the terms stated on the invoice. Late payment may attract interest and collection costs to the extent permitted by law.</li>
    <li>Deposits secure scheduling and materials procurement. Refundability is set out in your contract.</li>
    <li>We do not store card details.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Licensing and insurance</h2>
  <p>
    Electrical, construction and roofing work is performed by appropriately licensed personnel and we
    carry insurance and bonding as required in the jurisdictions in which we operate. Documentation
    is available on request and is supplied with proposals.
  </p>

  <h2>Scheduling and access</h2>
  <p>
    Work depends on safe site access, permit issuance, utility scheduling and weather. We will keep
    you informed of changes. Delays caused by third parties, including permitting authorities and
    utilities, are outside our control.
  </p>

  <h2>Warranties</h2>
  <p>
    Workmanship and equipment warranties are set out in your contract and in the manufacturer
    documentation supplied at handover. Warranties may be voided by unauthorised modification,
    neglect of required maintenance, or damage from causes outside normal use.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The content, branding and artwork on this site belong to {site.legalName} and may not be
    reproduced without permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses
    arising from use of this website. Nothing here limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited,
    including for death or personal injury caused by negligence.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    This site may link to third-party resources. We do not control those sites and are not
    responsible for their content or practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the state of {site.address.region}, United States, without
    regard to conflict of law principles.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or
    <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
